From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Opaniuk <igor.opaniuk@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:21:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] fix(qti): take the SPMI arbiter base from the SoC
 definitions

The SPMI arbiter driver hardcodes the hoya register addresses, but
shikra builds it too, with the arbiter at 0x01C00000 instead of
0x0C400000 (per ipcat: PMIC_ARB_REG_ADDRn at 0x01C40900 and the
PMIC_ARB_CHNLn registers at 0x01E00000, as on the other bruin SoCs).
On every PSCI SYSTEM_RESET and SYSTEM_OFF, which configure the PON
PS_HOLD function through the arbiter, shikra thus reads the APID map
from unmapped address space at 0x0C440900 and writes the SPMI command
word into the APPS MMU-500 secure configuration register
(APPS_SMMU_SCR0) at 0x0C600000.

Derive the register addresses from PMIC_ARB_BASE instead: shikra_def.h
already defines it, unused until now, and hoya_def.h gains it with the
address the driver used to hardcode, so the hoya platforms are
unchanged. The APID map and the channel registers lie at the same
offsets from the base on both SoCs.

Fixes: 0cc5324171e0
Change-Id: I613948ad84ca0b39a28d57c912f25f26627c7961
Link: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/55732
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Igor Opaniuk <igor.opaniuk@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/commit/62c968a0dc544b5cad48d88813b88b9ba7931479]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 plat/qti/common/src/spmi_arb.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 plat/qti/hoya/inc/hoya_def.h   |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/qti/common/src/spmi_arb.c b/plat/qti/common/src/spmi_arb.c
index 4213ed1b3..06e81d496 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/src/spmi_arb.c
+++ b/plat/qti/common/src/spmi_arb.c
@@ -8,19 +8,24 @@
 #include <drivers/delay_timer.h>
 #include <lib/mmio.h>
 
+#include <platform_def.h>
 #include <spmi_arb.h>
 
-#define REG_APID_MAP(apid)	(0x0C440900U + sizeof(uint32_t) * apid)
+/* Arbiter core and channel registers, at fixed offsets from PMIC_ARB_BASE */
+#define REG_ARB_CORE		(PMIC_ARB_BASE + 0x40000U)
+#define REG_ARB_CHNL(apid)	(PMIC_ARB_BASE + 0x200000U + 0x10000U * apid)
+
+#define REG_APID_MAP(apid)	(REG_ARB_CORE + 0x900U + sizeof(uint32_t) * apid)
 #define NUM_APID		((0x1100U - 0x900U) / sizeof(uint32_t))
 
 #define PPID_MASK		(0xfffU << 8)
 
-#define REG_ARB_CMD(apid)	(0x0C600000U + 0x10000U * apid)
+#define REG_ARB_CMD(apid)	(REG_ARB_CHNL(apid) + 0x0U)
 /* These are opcodes specific to this SPMI arbitrator, *not* SPMI commands. */
 #define OPC_EXT_WRITEL		0
 #define OPC_EXT_READL		1
 
-#define REG_ARB_STATUS(apid)	(0x0C600008U + 0x10000U * apid)
+#define REG_ARB_STATUS(apid)	(REG_ARB_CHNL(apid) + 0x8U)
 #define ARB_STATUS_DONE		BIT(0)
 #define ARB_STATUS_FAILURE	BIT(1)
 #define ARB_STATUS_DENIED	BIT(2)
@@ -29,8 +34,8 @@
 /* Fake status to report driver errors. */
 #define ARB_FAKE_STATUS_TIMEOUT	BIT(8)
 
-#define REG_ARB_RDATA0(apid)	(0x0C600018U + 0x10000U * apid)
-#define REG_ARB_WDATA0(apid)	(0x0C600010U + 0x10000U * apid)
+#define REG_ARB_RDATA0(apid)	(REG_ARB_CHNL(apid) + 0x18U)
+#define REG_ARB_WDATA0(apid)	(REG_ARB_CHNL(apid) + 0x10U)
 
 static int addr_to_apid(uint32_t addr)
 {
diff --git a/plat/qti/hoya/inc/hoya_def.h b/plat/qti/hoya/inc/hoya_def.h
index 502a16351..0f344be16 100644
--- a/plat/qti/hoya/inc/hoya_def.h
+++ b/plat/qti/hoya/inc/hoya_def.h
@@ -149,6 +149,11 @@
 /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 #define QTI_PS_HOLD_REG				0x0C264000
 
+/*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
+/* PMIC SPMI arbiter base address                                             */
+/*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
+#define PMIC_ARB_BASE				0x0C400000
+
 /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 /* SOC hw version register */
 /*----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
